From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tempeste <tempeste@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:45:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] flashnext: bf16 prompt weights, YaRN at --tp 2, picture
 prompts riding rounds, route and draft dumps

bf16 weight copies for dense prompt projections, YaRN and the shared pool at --tp 2, picture prompts riding decode
rounds and resuming at the image cut, the vision tower skipped for pictures before a restored state, a default-off
expert route dump and batch-aware expert re-route, a draft dump with tools/vgate_fit.py, and beside pieces at low
stream counts and on a share of the SMs.

Changes, in the order they were made:
- flashnext: bf16 weight copies for the dense prompt projections (TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_BF16W)
- flashnext: YaRN and the shared pool at --tp 2
- flashnext: lane ledger says why each prompt call ran alone; TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_QUEUE queues waiting pieces
- fix(flashnext): a new engine starts from its field defaults, so beside is null
- flashnext: rank 1 guards its own memory under the shared pool at --tp 2
- feat(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_IMAGE_FAST lets picture prompts ride decode rounds and keep a state before the first
  picture
- test(flashnext-image-ride): compare the picture ride with the same round beside text, and gate windows on their
  verify only where Y_BF16 does not split them
- feat(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_DUMP writes one record per drafted position of a shared round's head windows,
  and tools/vgate_fit.py fits a verify gate from it
- feat(flashnext): default-off expert route dump and batch-aware expert re-route for shared decode rounds
- fix(pcache): with TF_FLASHNEXT_IMAGE_FAST, a picture removed resumes at the image cut and a changed question after a
  picture resumes past it
- feat(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_IMAGE_SKIP_KEPT runs the vision tower only for pictures past a restored kept state
- feat(server): the done line ends with images=N when the prompt holds pictures
- feat(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE_WHOLE and _MOST put read pieces beside the decode rounds at low stream
  counts
- feat(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE_SMS runs the beside piece on a green context's share of the SMs
- fix(flashnext): route dump and expert re-route take main decode layers only; draft dump keys each stream

Flags this patch adds (a flag's default is its unset value; unset leaves the engine as it was
before the flag, and a knob named under another flag only matters when that flag is on):
- TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_DUMP takes an absolute file path and _MIB a cap of 1 to 16384 MiB (256 unset), refuses anything
  else and leaves the identity alone
- TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_DUMP_MIB=<MiB> (with TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_DUMP): the dump's size cap, default 256.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_EXPERT_REROUTE is off unset or 0, takes K0,KP,MIN in range, refuses anything else and sets bits 54-63
  with its settings' digest
- TF_FLASHNEXT_IMAGE_FAST is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses anything else and sets tp_flags bit 53 alone
- TF_FLASHNEXT_IMAGE_SKIP_KEPT is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses anything else and leaves tp_flags alone
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE_MOST is 0 (no limit) unset, takes 0 to 1024 decoders, refuses anything else, sets no
  tp_flags bit and needs TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE_SMS is off unset or 0, takes a count or a share of the SMs, refuses anything else, sets no
  tp_flags bit and needs TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE_WHOLE is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses anything else, sets no tp_flags bit and needs
  TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_BESIDE
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_QUEUE is off unset or 0, a depth of 1 to 8, refuses anything else, sets no tp_flags bit and needs
  TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_LAST
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_BF16W: added by the change "bf16 weight copies for the dense prompt projections
  (TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_BF16W)".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_BF16W_MIN_ROWS=<rows> (with TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_BF16W): the smallest call that takes the bf16
  weight copies, default 256.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUTE_DUMP is off unset or empty, takes an absolute path and a cap in MiB, refuses anything else and
  stays out of tp_flags
- TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUTE_DUMP_MB=<MiB> (with TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUTE_DUMP): the dump's size cap, default 1024.
